  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-03-15T07:29:31.974Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "OnExit events will trigger for each individual object exiting the collider regardless of if the Trigger Individuals flag is set or not. This contrasts against the OnEnter behavior which only triggers for the first object that enters the collider when the Trigger Individuals flag is off.\n\nGiven the behavior of the OnEnter event, I would expect that the having the Trigger Individual flag off for OnExit events would only trigger the event when the last object exits the collider.\n\nThis feature is mainly important for if you wanted to have a bunch of objects that you can pickup and move around freely, but have them respawn if they all exceed a certain boundary.",
